        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim Howard, Des McAleenan, John Berner, Tony Meola, Jonny Walker\n- Organizations: Colorado Rapids, United States national team, Manchester United, Major League Soccer\n- Roles: Goalkeepers, coach, captain, MVP\n- Events: 2009 MLS All-Star Game\n\nFacts:\n- Tim Howard was born on March 6, 1979.\n- John Berner was born on February 14, 1991.\n- Des McAleenan coached goalkeeper Tim Howard before Tim Howard moved to Manchester United.\n- Des McAleenan also coached United States full internationals Tony Meola and Jonny Walker.\n- In the 2009 MLS All-Star Game, Everton goalkeeper Tim Howard saved three kicks in the shootout and was named the match MVP.\n- Tim Howard is an American soccer player who captains Colorado Rapids and plays as a goalkeeper for the United States national team.\n- John Berner is an American professional soccer player who plays as a goalkeeper for Colorado Rapids in Major League Soccer.",
